			<div class="content" id="post-content-4817012">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Romance/Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Normal conprocs+desc followed by several interview logs, ending with a series of audio transcripts.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX is a large, open, underground area, slightly larger than a typical sports gym. On Friday, Saturday and Sunday nights after 8 P.M., the interior of SCP-XXXX will anomalously become that of a nightclub. A large crowd, as well as a full staff and a DJ group, will appear within the building, where a rave will occur. If left undisturbed, the sequence of events that occur during the party will be exactly the same throughout each Friday-Sunday cycle. Interfering with the party will change the series of events, but only for that Friday-Sunday sequence. The people inside of the SCP are unaware of their limited period of existence and behave as if they were progressing with their lives normally.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative of this SCP centers around several interviews and audio logs. The interviews are with participants in the party and will provide exposition as to what the party is and the identities of the DJ group. The party is the last showing of DJ group <em>After Hours</em>, a group that was very well-known in the clubbing scene. The group has been performing for about 2 years and can no longer financially support themselves through performing at clubs. The audio logs will explore the relationship between the two members of After Hours, developing their characters and showing their love for their work. In the end, it's revealed that the anomaly is a time capsule of some sort, meant to store the greatest moments of their lives.</p>
<p>The Foundation will passively interview the party-goers in order to obtain info on the two DJs, who are going to be labeled as a couple of PoIs (or maybe just a small GoI). They intend to track them down and interrogate them, but that may not be so easy. (This will mostly serve as a motive for the Foundation to collect the info necessary for the narrative).</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> Two people's love for music and each other is detailed as a faint memory through an eternal party. The anomaly is their happy ending- getting to perform for their fans and themselves until the end of time. It's an homage to parties and the love of musical expression that takes the reader on an emotional ride.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Let me know if the narrative needs to be clarified more. All questions and crit are appreciated!</p>

