<blockquote>
<p>The narrative of this SCP centers around several interviews and audio logs. The interviews are with participants in the party and will provide exposition as to what the party is and the identities of the DJ group.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My, concern is that there's not a lot of stakes to this information: I'm concerned this will feel like a bunch of kinda tedious interview logs that just deliver exposition about the SCP without there being some reason for a reader to be invested in the information.</p>
<p>The angle of this being a time capsule of sorts is kinda sweet and I like it, but it feels like it might need more of a narrative hook to get us there: it feels like perhaps some kind of conflict would really help; even if it's just the Foundation trying to understand how this works so they can stop it because the noise is like, in danger of breaching the veil or something? Or even just for there to be some kinda emotional arc to the story of the to After Hours DJs here?</p>

							</div>

								
					
