<blockquote>
<p>The majority of the issue here seems to be in keeping the article engaging throughout the narrative, so I'm going to try and think of some ways to keep it engaging. If you have any ideas/suggestions other than your previous ones, please, let me know!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My general thoughts for figuring this out is to consider what the stakes are: like, if the Foundation doesn't find out, what happens? If they do find out, what happens? Like, so you really have a feel for what the weight of the information is.</p>
<p>This might work more out of universe too: like, maybe there's not a lot of consequences for the Foundation but a reader can be hooked into really wanting to know more somehow? Usually this is easier if there's consequences in universe though.</p>
<p>Alternatively: maybe there's a character arc for the PoV character that's really important here: like, this experience changes them in some way and that change is what's driving our interest forwards?</p>

