														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820501">
									

<p>So I think this would be rather more interesting as a tale, from the perspective of two people experiencing this anomaly and growing to love it as an escape&#8230; it could still hit those tonal notes you're looking for.</p>
<p>As an anomaly the SCP Foundation has contained, I would be less than interested. Like Sqyd, I feel there's no real stakes and this isn't much of a threat to normalcy or to public safety. This seems like the sort of thing they'd note in their records and then maybe follow up if it exacerbated in some way.</p>
<p>What would they ever research? I really do think a personal tale about &quot;Two people's love for music and each other is detailed as a faint memory through an eternal party&quot; would be more compelling.</p>

							</div>

								
					
