					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ancient-five" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5089398); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5089398&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605806666" alt="Ancient Five" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5089398)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ancient-five" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5089398); return false;" >Ancient Five</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605637960 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Nov 2020 18:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820973">
									

<p>The idea of this being a tale is interesting. I could probably retain the same narrative that I intend to present in this SCP article through a Tale, although it would likely require more in-depth writing than expressing it through the article would. I'd like to stick with the idea of having it be created by the two- it would fit my idea of their origins better- but the idea of finding it could also work for this object, yeah. Rewriting this as a tale is definitely possible, though, and I'll keep this in mind.</p>
<p>I noted in one of my responses to Sqyd that the Foundation may find the DJ pair to be a small GoI or a couple PoIs. That would explain them researching the object itself, as well as interacting with its inhabitants. I feel that this may be somewhat tenuous as an explanation, but I think it would work overall. They would mostly be attempting to gain information on the Djs and where they might be now, mostly in order to find them and probably question them about the anomaly. It's not especially urgent information, but could potentially be good to know.</p>
<p>The stakes of the anomaly itself would be hard to create. Sure, there are options (i.e. anyone in the anomaly at the end of its cycle becomes trapped inside forever), but most of them feel like they would stray from the anomaly's purpose. I'll brainstorm this for a while and see if I can come up with anything.</p>

							</div>

								
					
